        "content": "WHAT THE PERSON SEES BEFORE BETTING (you get exactly this; the person sees the same text on screen)\nTHE PASTED CODE (JavaScript, the whole file, lines 1-10):\n 1| export function tierCounts(scores) {\n 2|   const counts = { A: 0, B: 0, C: 0 };\n 3|   for (const s of scores) {\n 4|     if (s >= 90) counts.A++;\n 5|     else if (s > 75) counts.B++;\n 6|     else counts.C++;\n 7|   }\n 8|   return counts;\n 9| }\n10| \n\nWHAT ATLAS WILL DO\nAtlas calls tierCounts([90,75,76,100]).\n\nHOW ATLAS RUNS IT\n- Atlas calls the function once, in a sandbox: no network, no files, no packages.\n- A stand-in is a fake function Atlas passes in; its answer on each call is fixed in advance, as described above.\n- Atlas's clock is virtual: waits (timers, sleeps, a stand-in's delay) cost no real time. It starts at 2026-01-01T00:00:00Z. Atlas watches for at most 30000 ms of virtual time.\n- How the call ends is one of \"returned\", \"threw\", \"never_settled\" (still waiting with nothing left that could wake it) or \"still_running_at_watch_limit\" (still working when the watch limit ran out).\n- The returned value is compared as JSON with keys sorted.\n\nQUESTIONS (written by plain code; a person answers the same ones)\n1. measures \"outcome\": Atlas calls tierCounts([90,75,76,100]). What does tierCounts do?\n   answer: {\"kind\":\"enum\",\"value\":<one of \"returned\" | \"threw\" | \"never_settled\" | \"still_running_at_watch_limit\">,\"options\":[\"returned\",\"threw\",\"never_settled\",\"still_running_at_watch_limit\"]}\n2. measures \"returnedJson\": Atlas calls tierCounts([90,75,76,100]). If tierCounts returns, what value does it return, as JSON?\n   answer: {\"kind\":\"json\",\"value\":<any JSON value>}\n3. measures \"virtualMs\": Atlas calls tierCounts([90,75,76,100]). How long until tierCounts returns or throws, in ms of Atlas's virtual clock?\n   answer: {\"kind\":\"number\",\"value\":<number>,\"tolerancePct\":10,\"unit\":\"ms\"}\n\nTASK\nBet on what this experiment's run will measure:\nexactly one bet per question, using the answer JSON shown for it.\nGive your best prediction for every question. Decline only if you cannot form any prediction at all; if you decline, say why.\nTo decline, bet {\"kind\":\"declined\",\"reason\":\"unknown: <why>\"}.\n\nReturn only this JSON object:\n{\"bets\": [{\"measures\": \"<field>\", \"answer\": {...}, \"rationale\": \"<one or two sentences>\"}]}"
